{% comment %}
  TEMPORARY exploration section.

  Cycles the hero lockup's "Obsessed" word through 50 open-licensed (OFL /
  Apache-2.0, all from Google Fonts) cursive/script faces so we can compare them
  live on the PR preview and pick the closest to the (proprietary, unembeddable)
  Brush Script MT look. The candidates are grouped in the label: [A] brush /
  bold informal (closest to Brush Script MT), [B] rounded / friendly, [C]
  flowing / signature, [D] elegant / formal calligraphy. Each candidate is a
  tiny text-subset woff2 (glyphs for "Obsessed" only), staged as
  assets/tmp-<slug>.woff2.

  Manual prev / next controls (arrow buttons, or the Left/Right arrow keys)
  drive it; there is no auto-advance. This pass shows each raw face with no
  faux-bold; once a face is chosen we bring weight-tuning back for that one.

  When a face is chosen: fetch its full (non-subset) woff2, wire it into
  .hero-lockup__word in hero.liquid with its OFL/Apache license in assets/,
  delete this section and its templates/index.json entry, and sweep all
  assets/tmp-*.woff2. Nothing else references this.
{% endcomment %}

